<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM6-DEAD-DISPATCHER-NAMED-AS-CANONICAL-PATH>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM6-DEAD-DISPATCHER-NAMED-AS-CANONICAL-PATH" ;
  triage:title "am6-closure-proof.md's singular-write-path QA handoff names dead code for 3 of 6 roles" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-AM6-1 (BLOCKING-1, ruthless-boundary-qa, independently confirmed via direct grep): docs/plans/phase-am/am6-closure-proof.md's 'QA handoff: singular production write path' -- the central architectural deliverable of AM.6 -- names DaemonRequestDispatcher's ApiRouter dispatch, MessageWriter boundary, and run_received_hook (all in atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/dispatch.rs and peer_delivery_router.rs) for 3 of its 6 roles. These are dead code: DaemonRequestDispatcher::new has zero non-test call sites anywhere in the codebase; atm-daemon-bootstrap constructs only StorageAndNudgeRouter (a different type, in atm-http-runtime); crates/atm-http-runtime/src/message_handler.rs explicitly documents that canonical_api_router 'never invokes the frozen daemon dispatcher.' This dead parallel dispatch stack should have been deleted in AM.3 per AM.1's own caller-before-callee ordering rule once its callers were removed -- its survival to AM.6 and being cited as the phase's own proof of a single canonical path is the exact failure mode AM is designed to prevent. Fix requires: (a) rewrite the QA handoff to name the actual live write path (StorageAndNudgeRouter and its real dispatch/write/received-hook implementation in atm-http-runtime), and (b) delete the dead DaemonRequestDispatcher/ApiRouter/MessageWriter/run_received_hook code from atm-daemon, with a negative guard preventing its reintroduction." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "dead-code-boundary-violation" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-11T00:44:46Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AM-S6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-11T00:44:02Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-11T01:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Fixed @ c07a3a79: DaemonRequestDispatcher's ApiRouter/MessageWriter/PostWriteRouter/run_received_hook impls and their modules (runtime_health.rs, dispatch.rs, peer_delivery_router.rs) are physically deleted from crates/atm-daemon/src; am6-closure-proof.md's QA handoff now names StorageAndNudgeRouter/CanonicalWriteHandler. Reachability independently re-verified by 3 reviewers (req-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa, arch-qa) tracing atm-daemon-bootstrap's actual construction call graph through to all three HTTP listeners. A new enabled, mutation-tested negative guard (dead-daemon-dispatch category) prevents reintroduction." ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AM6-DEAD-DISPATCHER-NAMED-AS-CANONICAL-PATH/AM6-DEAD-DISPATCHER-NAMED-AS-CANONICAL-PATH/AM6-QA1-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

